Abstract = {With technology development approach to cleaning changed as well. The
   vacuum cleaner robot market suggests a wide choice of different models.
   Choosing the model with optimal price, engine power, noise level, and
   other significant parameters is troublesome. In this case, MCDA methods
   can be helpful, which also proofs that it can also be used to daily
   decision problems.
   In this paper, two of them are used: the COMET and the TOPSIS. The first
   step is to analyze the subject and determine characteristic criteria.
   The second - selecting some market models which would be ranked. The
   third - normalize data for the TOPSIS method. After these preparations,
   both methods can be applied to our models, and alternatives can be
   ranked. Two MCDA methods were selected to compare MCDA methods based on
   the distance to reference objects. This simple study case also shows
   that the COMET method returns more accurate results and presents the
   advantages of this method. In conclusion, further research directions
   are shortly discussed. (C) 2021 The Authors. Published by Elsevier B.V.
