Note = {16th International KES Conference on Intelligent Decision Technologies,
   Santa Cruz, PORTUGAL, JUN 19-21, 2024},
Abstract = {Geographic information systems are a universal source of up-to-date
   information about the region. Moreover, this information is
   heterogeneous (from spatial data to descriptive data) and is used when
   making decisions by all possible stakeholders: economic partners,
   enterprises, other regions, e-government. In this regard, the urgent
   task is to make a decision on regular updating of the GIS, based on
   various factors (from technical to economic, socio-cultural and
   organizational). To automate and simplify this task we propose a method
   and a corresponding decision support software service for linguistic
   multi-criteria choice among multiple design alternatives. Our method and
   prototype are based on a hierarchy of cross-disciplinary criteria and
   ontology-based mechanisms (for the dynamic GUI customization) which
   reflect the concept of crisisology.},
