Year = {2023},
Volume = {30},
Number = {9},
Pages = {3067-3089},
Month = {DEC 1},
Abstract = {Purpose Explainable artificial intelligence (XAI) has importance in
   several industrial applications. The study aims to provide a comparison
   of two important methods used for explainable AI algorithms.
   Design/methodology/approach In this study multiple criteria has been
   used to compare between explainable Ranked Area Integrals (xRAI) and
   integrated gradient (IG) methods for the explainability of AI
   algorithms, based on a multimethod phase-wise analysis research design.
   Findings The theoretical part includes the comparison of frameworks of
   two methods. In contrast, the methods have been compared across five
   dimensions like functional, operational, usability, safety and
   validation, from a practical point of view. Research
   limitations/implications A comparison has been made by combining
   criteria from theoretical and practical points of view, which
   demonstrates tradeoffs in terms of choices for the user.
   Originality/value Our results show that the xRAI method performs better
   from a theoretical point of view. However, the IG method shows a good
   result with both model accuracy and prediction quality.},
